CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ parameter types deduced: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The code type of a member function lists the implicit object parameter
first; deduction compared the pattern's first parameter A against it, so
A was deduced as the `this' pointer type (or the pack had one element too
many) and the partial specializations did not match.
